<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sandakan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elopura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sandakan is a city on the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a>, Malaysia. Founded in 1879 and renamed from Elopura, it was the capital of British North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> from 1884 until much of it was destroyed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, when the Japanese held prisoners of war there; the Sandakan death marches began from its camp. The capital then moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kota-kinabalu">Jesselton</a>, now Kota Kinabalu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sandakan.jpg" alt="Sandakan" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CEphoto, Uwe Aranas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sandakan_Sabah_MajlisPerbandaranSandakan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
